<title>UK: Argos falls amid talk of broker downgrade.</title>
<headline>Argos falls amid talk of broker downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in stores group Argos Plc slid in early trading amid talk of a cut in profit forecasts by HSBC James Capel, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0751 GMT the shares were trading 22-1/2p lower at 774p.</p>
<p>&quot;We've heard there's been a downgrade by James Capel. Capels are saying costs are higher than expected and have cut forecasts for this year and next,&quot; said one trader.  </p>
<p>James Capel analysts were not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
